# Placeholder certificate for a documentation tenant. Not the real one.
#
# This is a self-signed certificate generated with openssl (rsa:2048, ten
# years, CN=placeholder-entra-signing.example.com) whose private key was
# written to the null device and never existed on disk: it is public key
# material that signs nothing and is trusted by nothing. It stands in for
# the file a real cell carries so the fragment beside it can read it with
# file() and the stack can be planned offline.
#
# The real file is the enterprise application's SAML signing certificate,
# downloaded in Base64 form from the Entra portal (the okta-workforce
# application in the corp entra-enterprise-apps cell, Single sign-on, SAML
# Certificates, Certificate (Base64)), or the value output of that cell's
# signing certificate resource. Replace this whole file with that download;
# openssl and the idp-saml module both read only the text between the BEGIN
# and END CERTIFICATE lines, so these comment lines are ignored either way.
